# Line endings are normalised to LF for every text file this repo tracks. Without this, a Windows
# checkout applies core.autocrlf and converts LF to CRLF on the fly, which then conflicts with
# .editorconfig's end_of_line = lf and fails `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` only on the
# Windows CI runner - exactly the kind of platform-specific failure that is invisible from Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.traineddata binary
*.dll binary
*.pdf binary
